---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import SoftwareApplicationSchema from '../components/schema/SoftwareApplicationSchema.astro';
import FAQPageSchema from '../components/schema/FAQPageSchema.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const featuresFaqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does Pour Picks work with all bourbon bottles?',
    a: 'Pour Picks covers American whiskey: bourbon, rye, Tennessee whiskey, wheat whiskey and American single malt. The label scanner works on store picks and bottles with no barcode. If a bottle isn\'t in the catalog or the scan doesn\'t match, you can search by hand or save the bottle as your own.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Pour Picks free to use?',
    a: 'Yes. The free version holds 5 owned bottles and 5 label scans, and you can browse the catalog, take the Bourbon DNA quiz and write reviews. Cask Club is $5.99 a month or $49.99 a year. It removes both limits and adds Wishlist and Finished shelves and Precision Match. Apple handles billing, so your payment details never reach my servers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the AI label scanner?',
    a: 'Point your iPhone camera at the front label and the AI reads the distillery, expression and proof, then matches it to a bottle in the catalog. You can correct anything it got wrong before the bottle goes in your cellar, or search by hand instead.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does Pour Picks recommend bourbon?',
    a: 'Bourbon DNA is a short quiz that learns whether you lean sweet or spicy, easy sipper or cask strength, then names the bottle to buy next with the reasons. Bourbon Concierge takes a bottle you love and finds the closest matches. Pour Tonight picks a bottle to open from your own cellar, weighted to your palate. Cask Club adds Precision Match: 10 questions, your top 10 bottles, and why each one fits.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Features"
  description="What Pour Picks does: AI label scanning, Bourbon DNA, Pour Tonight, Bourbon Concierge, reviews, cellar value, and what Cask Club adds."
  path="/features"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <SoftwareApplicationSchema featureList="Bourbon cellar tracker, AI label scanner, taste quiz, taste-matched recommendations, tasting journal, Pour Tonight feature" />
    <FAQPageSchema faqs={featuresFaqs} />
    <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={[{ name: 'Features', url: `${SITE.url}/features` }]} />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png" />
  </Fragment>

  <header class="dept-masthead">
    <p class="brand">{SITE.name}</p>
    <h1>Inside the app</h1>
    <p class="dept-lede">Six parts of the app, in about the order you'd use them, from your first scan to what your shelf is worth.</p>
  </header>

  <ol class="ledger">
    <li class="ledger-entry">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">01</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Cellar</span>
        <span class="ledger-spec">Owned &middot; Wishlist &middot; Finished</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>Your cellar</h2>
        <p>Every bottle is filed by distillery, expression, proof, age and fill level. The free version holds 5 owned bottles. Cask Club removes that limit and adds Wishlist and Finished shelves for what you're hunting and what you've emptied. When you can't decide what to open, Pour Tonight picks a bottle from your cellar, weighted to your palate.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="ledger-entry">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">02</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Catalog</span>
        <span class="ledger-spec">Bourbon &middot; Rye &middot; Tennessee &middot; Wheat &middot; Malt</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>The whole American shelf</h2>
        <p>Browse American whiskey by distillery, age, proof or price, or open it up to world spirits. Bottles list the mash bill and flavor tags, and you can add one to your cellar from there. Every bottle page lists food pairings, free for everyone. I publish some of the pairing data on the site as <a href="/pairings">bottle pairing guides</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="ledger-entry ledger-entry--feature">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">03</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Label scan</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>Scan the label</h2>
        <p class="ledger-stat">Works on store picks and bottles with no barcode.</p>
        <p>Point your camera at the front label and the AI reads the distillery, expression and proof, then finds the bottle in the catalog. You can fix anything it got wrong before it goes in your cellar. If the bottle isn't in the catalog, save it as your own. The free version includes 5 scans, and every add has a 4.5-second undo.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="ledger-entry">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">04</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Palate</span>
        <span class="ledger-spec">Bourbon DNA &middot; Concierge &middot; Precision Match</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>What to buy next</h2>
        <p>Bourbon DNA is a short quiz that learns whether you lean sweet or spicy, easy sipper or cask strength. Then it names the bottle to buy next and gives you the reasons. Bourbon Concierge starts from a bottle you already love and finds the closest matches. Cask Club adds Precision Match, which asks 10 questions and gives you your top 10 bottles and why each one fits.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="ledger-entry">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">05</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Reviews</span>
        <span class="ledger-spec">Nose &middot; Palate &middot; Finish</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>Rate every pour</h2>
        <p>Give each pour an overall rating plus separate marks for nose, palate and finish. You can note how you took it (neat, rocks, water, cocktail), the pour size, and anything else in your own words. Reviews are free for everyone, and your rating counts toward the average other collectors see on that bottle.</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="ledger-entry">
      <div class="ledger-index">
        <span class="ledger-no">06</span>
        <span class="ledger-dept">Value</span>
        <span class="ledger-spec">MSRP, or what you paid</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-body">
        <h2>What the shelf is worth</h2>
        <p>Your cellar total updates with every bottle you add. Each bottle starts at MSRP, and you can change it to what you paid. If you own more than one of something, you can set the count and the total includes each one.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <section class="closing">
    <h2 class="section-title">Something off?</h2>
    <p class="cta-body">
      If something in the app looks wrong, email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> and I'll take a look.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="cta" href={SITE.appStoreUrl}>Download on iOS</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
